== TML-3 Detection Protocol ==

All three independent mechanisms are deployed simultaneously:

# '''HRV arm:''' PPG sensor at mastoid; RMSSD computed in real time at 4 Hz. Compare active vs sham [[Psi Stabilizer]] condition. Primary endpoint.
# '''Back-EMF arm:''' Bifilar coil in receive mode; lock-in amplifier at <math>\omega_0 = 40</math> kHz; 1 Hz bandwidth. Compare active vs sham. Secondary endpoint.
# '''Q-shift arm:''' VNA probe coupled to shell; measure <math>\omega_0</math> and Q_L continuously. Compare operator-present vs empty-shell. Tertiary endpoint.

'''Cross-validation criterion:''' A positive result at TML-3 requires the primary endpoint (HRV) to be significant at <math>p < 0.05</math> after Bonferroni correction AND at least one secondary/tertiary endpoint to show a consistent direction of effect. Agreement across independent mechanisms significantly reduces the probability of false positive from any single artefact.

== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== ψ Charge as an Individual Biometric ===

The biological detection sensitivity scales as <math>p\,|\nabla\psi|</math> where <math>p</math> is the operator's ψ charge. If different operators have systematically different <math>p</math> values (varying with training, genetics, or physiological factors), RMSSD sensitivity to the same ψ field would vary between operators. This would manifest as operator-to-operator variability in TML-3 effect sizes beyond what RMSSD noise alone predicts.

Measuring this variability across the TML-3 cohort and correlating with training history constitutes a test of whether ψ charge is a stable individual biometric.

